    "selection_rationale": "Our primary peer group consists of large U.S.-based, stand-alone, publicly traded companies in the technology, media, and internet services industries that, in the People and Compensation Committee\u2019s view, compete with Apple for executive talent. Commensurate with Apple\u2019s size and scope, the People and Compensation Committee reviews Mr. Cook\u2019s total target compensation against the annualized total target CEO pay of our primary peer group, focusing on the 80th to 90th percentiles of peer CEO pay when setting Mr. Cook\u2019s pay. Other than for Mr. Cook, the People and Compensation Committee does not",
